<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:32:37Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Flavio Bolsonaro: In the name of the father, sons, and holy ideology</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed4c4ee8ee8de412daa922898eb749d27b3a7fd7bc6e0ebb2c9105d163c22e0a</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:32:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T09:48:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261003-flavio-bolsonaro-in-the-name-of-the-father-sons-and-holy-ideology--9892326d1899.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261003-flavio-bolsonaro-in-the-name-of-the-father-sons-and-holy-ideology" /><summary type="html">The first round of Brazil’s presidential election on Sunday pits two well-known names in the political ring: Lula vs. Bolsonaro. But it’s not former president Jair Bolsonaro facing off against the incumbent head of state – it’s his eldest son, Flavio Bolsonaro. He’s less charismatic than his father but just as ideologically radical as the family patriarch.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil’s Lula gears up for ‘last dance’ with run for fourth presidential term</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:10a4fd6202eca46e2178caf745d16910dfd674f47694fafea8262c029352af95</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T16:20:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261002-brazil-s-lula-gears-up-for-last-dance-with-run-for-fourth-presidential-term--5b44a3117a30.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261002-brazil-s-lula-gears-up-for-last-dance-with-run-for-fourth-presidential-term" /><summary type="html">President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva will stand for re-election in Brazil on Sunday. At 80, the former steelworker hopes to capitalise on his popularity and economic successes to win a fourth term in office but is neck-and-neck in the polls with far-right rival Flavio Bolsonaro.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil: Who is presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:28ab24aa7c6c1114124ae262351e9f96c2b34148e087243bbec2d670f312080e</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T15:06:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-brazil-who-is-presidential-candidate-flavio-bolsonaro--529bdce9ea36.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-brazil-who-is-presidential-candidate-flavio-bolsonaro" /><summary type="html">He was still relatively unknown in Brazil just a few months ago. The 45-year-old senator is now neck and neck with incumbent President Lula in the polls for the upcoming presidential election. Flavio Bolsonaro's victory would add Brazil to the long list of Latin American countries that have shifted to the right or far right in recent months.</summary></entry><entry><title>The Cornell 7: Allegations spark fury over gang rape culture</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1af30c35c7560684287faf5b759e75bdf655dcdba2848ccfdcb20bb30133bf16</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T14:39:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261002-the-cornell-7-allegations-spark-fury-over-gang-rape-culture--c1482a18eb2c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261002-the-cornell-7-allegations-spark-fury-over-gang-rape-culture" /><summary type="html">How allegations of a gang rape at an American Ivy League university have set social media alight, sparking widespread fury over the way colleges and universities handle sexual assault cases. Also the French parliament is currently debating a major new bill aimed at tackling violence against women and children. But does it go far enough? Annette Young asks Dr Andreea Gruev-Vintila, a social psychologist who assisted with the drafting of the legislation. Plus the king of Morocco names Marrakesh mayor, Fatima Ezzahra El Mansouri, as the country's first female prime minister.</summary><category term="The 51%" /></entry><entry><title>What the media got right and wrong about Cornell gang rape case</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3b8b4f41414739ba3f84157930301f669befcd8eeaff44638ab7cdfe1f68e429</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T13:53:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/scoop/20261002-what-the-media-got-right-and-wrong-about-cornell-gang-rape-case--863be3ca8b9a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/scoop/20261002-what-the-media-got-right-and-wrong-about-cornell-gang-rape-case" /><summary type="html">The alleged gang rape at America's Cornell University has shocked many people around the world and raised questions about institutional failure and toxic masculinity. The story was first broken by student journalists and national media soon followed, thrusting it in the spotlight. While there has been excellent reporting, the story has also exposed failures in how some pieces framed officials' statements alongside Jane Doe's allegations. We take a closer look in Scoop.</summary><category term="Scoop" /></entry><entry><title>Paraguay, a tax and political haven for Brazil's far right</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c7bf636f1fadbab337d672c52873f409c899e2c76d07ad68dd458949c78533c3</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T12:48:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261002-paraguay-a-tax-and-political-haven-for-brazil-s-far-right--68deff3b0c43.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261002-paraguay-a-tax-and-political-haven-for-brazil-s-far-right" /><summary type="html">Over the past five years, applications for residence permits submitted by Brazilians in Paraguay have more than doubled. Many of them are Bolsonaro supporters who are afraid October's presidential election will be won by incumbent leader Lula – whom they accuse of plunging the Latin American giant into an unprecedented economic crisis. FRANCE 24's Fanny Lothaire, Valeria Saccone and Mélanie Blondeau report, with Jan Onoszko.</summary><category term="Reporters" /></entry><entry><title>What's real and what's fake? How AI is impacting Brazil's election race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e66c157979a81db65ee4b72a242efacc96675dc5dd143ea231c171e73a5c858b</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T11:34:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261002-what-s-real-and-what-s-fake-how-ai-is-impacting-brazil-s-election-race--0b74a4095735.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261002-what-s-real-and-what-s-fake-how-ai-is-impacting-brazil-s-election-race" /><summary type="html">With just two days to go before the first round of Brazil's presidential election, artificial intelligence is taking centre stage, whether it's a deepfake avatar of former president Jair Bolsonaro to support his son's candidacy, or an AI-generated working-class female voter criticising President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva. According to the Brazilian intelligence agency, disinformation will be one of the main challenges of this election. Our correspondents report.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil's election: Lula or Bolsonaro Jr?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:abf57f4c962c03a5be2e7616fa5ee31814cc48ad5df4ff4afc1a72b61178bca5</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T11:04:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261002-brazil-s-election-lula-or-bolsonaro-jr--90417820582f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261002-brazil-s-election-lula-or-bolsonaro-jr" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Friday, October 2: We look at reactions in the French papers after high school blockades turned violent across France. We also look ahead to Brazil's two-round presidential election, which begins this weekend. The electoral campaign culminated with the cancellation of a presidential debate after both President Lula and his rival Flavio Bolsonaro pulled out. Finally, this year's Comedy Wildlife Awards finalists do not disappoint.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Lula and Bolsonaro’s mudslinging heats up ahead of weekend vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f8aed14c4df42302b090b8469130d8d2606b7c45c0b4154515b157f0175c2854</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T05:44:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261002-lula-and-bolsonaro-s-mudslinging-heats-up-ahead-of-weekend-vote--9b234ebd94f2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261002-lula-and-bolsonaro-s-mudslinging-heats-up-ahead-of-weekend-vote" /><summary type="html">The mudslinging between Brazil’s incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and his election rival, Flavio Bolsonaro, has heated up ahead of what is expected to be an extremely close vote this weekend. From stating loose rumours as facts, to taking comments completely out of their context, they are both doing everything they can to win a few more votes.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US continues to be 'a very significant partner', UN peacekeeping chief says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bfeee40e37e6a3c2deccc3bdd4d8c23af5be4b4e45f8ba720ac77db2e735e24c</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T13:14:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20261001-the-us-continue-to-be-a-very-significant-partner-un-peacekeeping-chief--b044ef9ba027.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261001-the-us-continue-to-be-a-very-significant-partner-un-peacekeeping-chief" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24, UN peacekeeping chief Jean-Pierre Lacroix said the US continues to be "a very significant partner", despite owing $3 billion to peacekeeping. With the UN forced to cut about 25 percent of its capacity, Lacroix defended missions that cost just 0.2 percent of global military spending: "Peacekeeping is a good deal really."</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>Convicted killer Christa Pike in ‘critical condition’ after two lethal injections fail to kill her</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bf53f75b692d6d6bfd01220f0bcffc029a507b796b7ad1412217aa3d842ce3fc</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T05:32:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261001-execution-of-convicted-us-killer-christa-pike-fails-despite-two-lethal-injections--aeb8f625e4e7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261001-execution-of-convicted-us-killer-christa-pike-fails-despite-two-lethal-injections" /><summary type="html">Christa Pike, who has been on death row in Tennessee for more than 30 years for torturing and murdering a classmate, was on Wednesday set to be executed, but the lethal injections meant to kill her failed. Pike was then transported to a medical facility, where her attorney says she remains in a "critical condition".</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>El Salvador sets date for 2027 presidential election as Bukele seeks third term</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1c4b0664df9d4d2e144a31175cb352b4bdfaaeb682c1bbc080aa591f0eebc650</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T02:32:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261001-el-salvador-sets-2027-presidential-election-as-nayib-bukele-seeks-third-term--90fb5878abea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261001-el-salvador-sets-2027-presidential-election-as-nayib-bukele-seeks-third-term" /><summary type="html">El Salvador will hold presidential elections on February 28, 2027, the electoral tribunal said Wednesday, opening the way for President Nayib Bukele to seek a third term after constitutional changes removed presidential term limits. Bukele has drawn praise for sharply reducing gang violence but faced criticism over rights abuses during his crackdown.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump renews calls for former Federal Reserve chief Jerome Powell's resignation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d224aa210918602c7c1e57d4d3fc50f611c058912877efce9167d504323dfff8</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T23:44:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260930-trump-renews-calls-for-former-federal-reserve-chief-jerome-powell-resignation--58eead028846.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260930-trump-renews-calls-for-former-federal-reserve-chief-jerome-powell-resignation" /><summary type="html">The Federal Reserve's watchdog on Wednesday found no grounds for a criminal referral over a roughly $1 billion cost overrun on renovations to the central bank's Washington buildings, while faulting project oversight. The findings prompted President Donald Trump to renew his call for former Fed chief Jerome Powell to resign.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Paramount takeover of Warner Bros. Discovery clears legal hurdle</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7696211dca11b7c4462134f0d0c86350888e050f691fe550ccc08a8ba7e4d1c5</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T22:19:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260930-paramount-takeover-of-warner-bros-discovery-clears-legal-hurdle--68378233ae13.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260930-paramount-takeover-of-warner-bros-discovery-clears-legal-hurdle" /><summary type="html">A federal judge on Wednesday approved a settlement clearing Paramount’s takeover of Warner Bros. Discovery after 12 US states challenged the deal on antitrust grounds. The agreement includes safeguards for CNN’s editorial independence and requires the merged studio to release at least 30 films a year for its first two years.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Pentagon’s Hegseth says 20 percent of US generals, admirals cut, ‘no fatties, no trannies’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b8800cfccfa4716597c3c3cbb07a95baf20ba0477b2d9ec61664df2bee2d2459</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T20:16:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260930-pentagon-s-hegseth-says-20-pct-of-us-generals-admirals-cut-no-fatties-no-trannies--b1447f73adbe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260930-pentagon-s-hegseth-says-20-pct-of-us-generals-admirals-cut-no-fatties-no-trannies" /><summary type="html">US Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth said Wednesday that his department had cut 20 percent of US admirals, generals and officers who did not fit his vision. "Simple translation of that: no fatties, no trannies, no beardos, no weirdos, no wimps, no radicals. Just warriors – just tough, ready, committed troops," he said.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Meet 'America': Trump's AI chatbot changes answers after challenging his claims</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9acf2db464479d5387ad7dda26e9f3b1757dc7f540a7cb43f8234c6974698558</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T20:08:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/meet-america-trump-s-ai-chatbot-changes-answers-after-challenging-his-claims-1--7d4ab69afaa6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/meet-america-trump-s-ai-chatbot-changes-answers-after-challenging-his-claims-1" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump has launched "America", an AI chatbot designed as a digital portal for US government information. But its responses appear to be changing. The chatbot initially challenged several of Trump's claims, including on the 2020 election and inflation, providing evidence and links. More recently, it has refused to answer some of the same questions. Other responses still contradict Trump, while some echo his views. Vedika Bahl tests the chatbot and its varying answers in Truth or Fake.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>US Supreme Court clears way for Tennessee execution of woman for murder</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5f80de66a3b59ad56c3621672c98037270ca7a1898f65e8cdc6d3ea3418a6a31</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T16:03:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260930-appeals-court-halts-execution-of-tennessee-woman-less-than-two-hours-before-lethal-injectio--883b9a62beca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260930-appeals-court-halts-execution-of-tennessee-woman-less-than-two-hours-before-lethal-injection" /><summary type="html">The US Supreme Court on Wednesday cleared the way for Tennessee to execute Christa Pike, 50, the state's first woman put to death in 200 years. The ruling came hours after a federal appeals court temporarily halted the lethal injection to consider claims that Pike's childhood sexual abuse was not adequately weighed at sentencing.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'Cornell won't, we will': Student journalists 'relentlessly' reporting on university rape</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:697a480ebc1616d070d7ce57e04874dc179f42415fa22f6f9de81bd00d411332</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T11:06:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260930-cornell-won-t-we-will-student-journalists-relentlessly-reporting-on-university-rape--316f2be7b7a1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260930-cornell-won-t-we-will-student-journalists-relentlessly-reporting-on-university-rape" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Wednesday, September 30: The Cornell University gang rape investigation reopens. But first: students and prisoners protest in Iran "in a rare show of dissent". Journalist Evan Gershkovich speaks about his 16 months in a Russian prison. Bonus: what can we do to be less lonely? Finally, Fat Bear Week has chosen its winner.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Ian Bremmer: 'We have passed peak Trump in terms of disruption on the global stage'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be2615f14020cddb7315319c444ae3b04f8b37e24940d63d93d4925f8e3626dd</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T07:15:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260930-ian-bremmer-we-have-passed-peak-trump-in-terms-of-disruption-on-the-global-stage--0f18ab749ec8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260930-ian-bremmer-we-have-passed-peak-trump-in-terms-of-disruption-on-the-global-stage" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Ian Bremmer, the American political scientist, author, and founder and president of Eurasia Group and GZERO Media. According to Bremmer, we may now be entering the autumn of the "Donroe Doctrine" and the MAGA era: an "America First" isolationist approach in which President Donald Trump envisions a return to "greatness" in Gilded Age fashion. But is this the America voters had envisioned?</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Trump’s tariffs loom over talks as G20 meets in US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:52df7f86040da69ef73ebdf38f4e91be51f509e6a4504164b4b8e8e8e09d9333</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T05:29:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260930-g20-meets-in-us-as-trump-s-tariffs-loom-over-talks--a1f96983ad0c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260930-g20-meets-in-us-as-trump-s-tariffs-loom-over-talks" /><summary type="html">Trade ministers of the Group of 20 are meeting in Milwaukee for two days of talks on Wednesday, but US President Donald Trump’s tariffs are expected to hang heavy over the talks. "Don't expect any breakthroughs," an analyst watching the event said.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US Supreme Court lifts restrictions on third-country deportations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0aa49c3407e5c1790baa25648edac8cc6909d6b55130c041801cf29b3aec50de</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T23:17:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260929-us-supreme-court-lifts-restrictions-on-third-country-deportations--2246aab0be9d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260929-us-supreme-court-lifts-restrictions-on-third-country-deportations" /><summary type="html">The US Supreme Court on Tuesday cleared the Trump administration to resume deporting migrants to countries other than their own while it considers the legality of the practice. The court’s conservative majority temporarily blocked safeguards requiring deportees to receive notice of where they would be sent and time to raise persecution concerns.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Public service announcement or Trump propaganda?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8e36130ef7387f35ecfed95eb7d94982631f78b87870f384246b3fb99aec4b72</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T20:56:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20260929-public-service-announcement-or-donald-trump-propaganda--6e88764ee389.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20260929-public-service-announcement-or-donald-trump-propaganda" /><summary type="html">The White House calls them public service announcements, like those used in past administrations. But almost everyone else doesn't agree, with three taxpayer-funded advertisements that glorify US President Donald Trump drawing criticism from across the partisan divide. Legal experts say the ads violate federal laws on government propaganda, as FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell explains in this edition of Truth or Fake.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>OpenAI cancels release of new artificial intelligence model over safety concerns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:07fb24bd291c863f9838d6cce621e8ebfac77c54693e284ca83e3ff5bf0e02d8</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T02:54:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260929-openai-cancels-release-new-ai-model-safety-concerns--342610ada246.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260929-openai-cancels-release-new-ai-model-safety-concerns" /><summary type="html">OpenAI will not release its latest artificial intelligence model, Astra 6.1, after internal tests found it fell short of safety standards, the maker of ChatGPT confirmed on Monday. The decision came ahead of a meeting of AI leaders at the White House Tuesday convened by US President Donald Trump and House Speaker Mike Johnson amid mounting controversy over the risks posed by rogue AI.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Argentina’s Milei threatens to sue UK over Falkland Islands oil project</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aaf0e517edbc688ad8c6c85747eea0722d67c18547dce32987c410a608f24783</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T02:13:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260929-argentina-milei-arbitration-falklands-oil-project--6c7f62fb9112.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260929-argentina-milei-arbitration-falklands-oil-project" /><summary type="html">Argentine President Javier Milei on Monday threatened to sue the UK over the Sea Lion oil project near the disputed Falkland Islands. Argentina claims sovereignty over the British-administered territory, where a 1982 war killed 255 British and 649 Argentine troops. Developers Navitas and Rockhopper say they hold valid British-issued exploration licences.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US prosecutors reopen Cornell university gang rape investigation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3e74048cc841b816d9f457b712fe2af1f097358b6e4ec802ec47132eb966a8af</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T00:04:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260929-us-prosecutors-cornell-university-gang-rape-investigation--ba1abd3dd231.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260929-us-prosecutors-cornell-university-gang-rape-investigation" /><summary type="html">US prosecutors reopened an investigation on Monday into an alleged 2024 gang rape at Cornell University after the woman involved accused the school of failing to punish those responsible adequately. In a lawsuit, she said seven Chi Phi fraternity members had drugged her with ketamine and assaulted her.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US deportations are triggering a 'cascade' of rights abuses, UN experts warn</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b34de2f2c1b1d72dbf53790dcb61884ae156baa606274e90b26a1a268949f2a7</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T18:01:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260928-us-trump-deportations-triggering-cascade-of-rights-abuses-un-experts-warn-forbidden-stories--010f924e89a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260928-us-trump-deportations-triggering-cascade-of-rights-abuses-un-experts-warn-forbidden-stories" /><summary type="html">The Trump administration's policy of deportating thousands of people to countries with which they have no links is "increasing risks of torture and ill-treatment and enforced disappearance", a panel of independent UN experts warned on Monday. An investigation by an international consortium of journalists including FRANCE 24 reporters determined last week that more than 25,000 third-country nationals had been deported by the end of August.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Great Black Hope: Pursuit of belonging 'becomes a kind of cancer that eats them from the inside out'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4b08070b7a5565f476335a525ed14421247294fa4a701298498498ab2b73c15c</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T11:37:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/great-black-hope-pursuit-of-belonging-becomes-a-kind-of-cancer-that-eats-them-from-the-inside-out--ca6f07533dd3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/great-black-hope-pursuit-of-belonging-becomes-a-kind-of-cancer-that-eats-them-from-the-inside-out" /><summary type="html">Eve Irvine is pleased to welcome award-winning author Rob Franklin, joining us to discuss Great Black Hope, his acclaimed debut novel exploring race, class, respectability and belonging. Franklin wanted to write about the worlds he had spent years observing since childhood: including how class and race shape even our most intimate relationships.  At its centre is David Smith, a young Black man from a Southern bourgeois family. His education, manners and connections give him access, but he is constantly aware of the possibility of being cast out. That tension led him to think about respectability politics and the psychological cost of constantly performing an acceptable version of oneself.</summary></entry><entry><title>The week in pictures: Trump hosts Xi, the pope visits France and floods ravage Thailand</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:63c9a8c854997864a2e26568c914ecc95057d821155fa730152105312e4d1274</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T10:05:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260927-the-week-in-pictures-trump-hosts-xi-the-pope-visits-france-and-floods-ravage-thailand--94b87d455e05.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260927-the-week-in-pictures-trump-hosts-xi-the-pope-visits-france-and-floods-ravage-thailand" /><summary type="html">From Pope Leo XIV's historic first visit to France to US President Donald Trump meeting China's President Xi Jinping to flooded streets in Bangkok, FRANCE 24 looks back at the week's most striking pictures.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Unusually powerful storm pummels northeast US with heavy rain, high winds</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:839c964c61e6844a143fdb34a96e43d795ae45ba9514633dda9a8052f1a695d1</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T15:08:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260926-unusually-powerful-storm-pummels-northeast-us-with-heavy-rain-high-winds--c49e19e43688.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260926-unusually-powerful-storm-pummels-northeast-us-with-heavy-rain-high-winds" /><summary type="html">A powerful storm unusual for this time of year intensified on Sunday over the northeastern United States, bringing torrential rain and powerful winds that cut off power to tens of thousands of people and killed one person, according to US media.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil's President Lula bans online betting ahead of presidential election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9d6e71ee6feb347f4baa9a7d2051407387a23e1f2528b255a7cae09c223a8b53</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T12:36:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/brazil-s-president-lula-bans-online-betting-ahead-of-presidential-election--48f3127e0de1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-s-president-lula-bans-online-betting-ahead-of-presidential-election" /><summary type="html">Brazil’s President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva on Friday signed an order banning fixed-odds betting just over a week ahead of the first round of the presidential election, in a move he said was designed to tackle the pervasive problem of families falling into debt.</summary></entry></feed>
